  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 2-Oxopomolic Acid and the CD276 antigen, mediated through the DNA polymerase iota enzyme. This relationship is supported by multiple independent pathways, all of which indicate that 2-Oxopomolic Acid targets DNA polymerase iota, which in turn is targeted by various compounds, including (6S,10S)-6,10,14-trimethylpentadecan-2-one and Guangsangon K. These compounds ultimately lead to the CD276 antigen. The consistent scores across the three paths (final_score=0.4616) suggest a strong, albeit indirect, relationship, with the DNA polymerase iota acting as a critical intermediary. The evidence highlights a mechanistic link between 2-Oxopomolic Acid and CD276 antigen through a series of targets, but the exact role of DNA polymerase iota in this pathway remains to be fully elucidated. The findings underscore the importance of targeting DNA polymerase iota as a potential strategy to modulate CD276 antigen activity.",
